[38;5;252m[1m## What diverged, and what I fixed[0m[0m
[0m[0m
The C is built by CMake with [1mno[22m [38;5;10mCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE[0m, i.e. [38;5;10m-O0[0m. The existing translation's float code had been written against [38;5;10m-O2[0m assumptions, so its comments about "GCC swaps these operands" were wrong for the binary actually produced. I re-derived the operand order from [38;5;10mobjdump[0m on the real [38;5;10m.so[0m and fixed three things in [38;5;10mtranslation/src/lib.rs[0m:[0m[0m
[0m[0m
